  "content": {
    "id": "p41-q51-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "51",
    "prompt": "Show that\n$$\\binom{p+q+r}{p}\\times\\binom{q+r}{q}=\\binom{p+q+r}{q}\\times\\binom{p+r}{p}.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "Both sides equal $\\dfrac{(p+q+r)!}{p!q!r!}$.\n\nExpand the combinations into factorials and cancel common factors.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\binom{p+q+r}{p}\\binom{q+r}{q}&=\\frac{(p+q+r)!}{p!(q+r)!}\\times\\frac{(q+r)!}{q!r!}\\\\\\binom{p+q+r}{p}\\binom{q+r}{q}&=\\frac{(p+q+r)!}{p!q!r!}\\\\\\binom{p+q+r}{p}\\binom{q+r}{q}&=\\frac{(p+q+r)!}{q!(p+r)!}\\times\\frac{(p+r)!}{p!r!}\\\\\\binom{p+q+r}{p}\\binom{q+r}{q}&=\\binom{p+q+r}{q}\\binom{p+r}{p}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 58
  },
